@startuml Smart-Contract Integrated State Machine
!theme vibrant
skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam roundcorner 15
skinparam state {
  BackgroundColor<<Initial>> #E8F5E9
  BackgroundColor<<Processing>> #FFF3E0
  BackgroundColor<<Waiting>> #E3F2FD
  BackgroundColor<<Success>> #C8E6C9
  BackgroundColor<<Error>> #FFCDD2
  BackgroundColor<<Contract>> #F3E5F5
  BorderColor #455A64
  FontSize 12
}

title Smart-Contract Integrated State Machine\n(Hybrid Pattern: Contract → Order Flow)

note as N_LEGEND
  **Two-Track State Machine:**

  **Track 1: Contract States** (Purple)
  Contract manages payment lifecycle

  **Track 2: Order States** (Original colors)
  Order manages fulfillment lifecycle

  **Key Innovation:**
  Order created ONLY when contract committed
end note

[*] --> BASKET_ACTIVE : User adds items

state BASKET_ACTIVE <<Initial>>
note right of BASKET_ACTIVE
  **Shopping Phase:**
  - User browsing, adding items
  - No contract yet
  - No order yet
  - Basket in session
end note

BASKET_ACTIVE --> CONTRACT_DRAFT : **Event:** CheckoutInitiatedEvent\n(User clicks "Place Order")

note on link
  **Contract-First Architecture:**

  Instead of creating order immediately,
  we create a CONTRACT first.

  Order created later when contract
  conditions are fulfilled.
end note

note as N_PHASE1
  **PHASE 1: CONTRACT LIFECYCLE (Pre-Order Phase)**
  Contract manages payment conditions before order creation
end note

state CONTRACT_DRAFT <<Contract>> {
  state "CONTRACT: DRAFT\n(Intent captured,\nconditions defined)" as CD

  note right of CD
    **Contract Created:**

    Contract record in database:
    - OXSTATE = 'draft'
    - OXORDERID = NULL ← No order yet!
    - OXBASKETDATA = {snapshot}
    - OXCONDITIONS = [
        {type: 'payment_authorized', status: 'pending'},
        {type: 'fraud_check', status: 'pending'},
        {type: 'stock_reserved', status: 'pending'}
      ]

    **What happens:**
    1. Basket snapshot captured (immutable)
    2. Conditions defined
    3. Contract saved to osc_payment_contract
    4. NO ORDER CREATED YET!
  end note
}

CONTRACT_DRAFT --> CONTRACT_PENDING : **Event:** ContractTransitionedToPendingEvent

state CONTRACT_PENDING <<Contract>> {
  state "CONTRACT: PENDING\n(Conditions being resolved)" as CP

  note right of CP
    **Parallel Condition Resolution:**

    Multiple handlers work in parallel:

    ├─ PaymentAuthorizationHandler
    │  → Calls provider API
    │  → Fulfills 'payment_authorized'
    │
    ├─ FraudCheckHandler
    │  → Runs fraud detection
    │  → Fulfills 'fraud_check'
    │
    └─ StockReservationHandler
       → Reserves inventory
       → Fulfills 'stock_reserved'

    Contract monitors:
    Are ALL conditions fulfilled?
  end note
}

CP : **State in DB:**
CP : OXSTATE = 'pending'
CP : OXORDERID = NULL
CP : OXCONDITIONS = [conditions being resolved...]

CONTRACT_PENDING --> CONTRACT_READY : **Event:** ContractConditionsFulfilledEvent\n(All conditions met)

note on link
  **Critical Transition:**

  Contract detected all conditions
  are now fulfilled.

  Contract automatically transitions
  to READY_TO_COMMIT state.

  This triggers order creation!
end note

CONTRACT_PENDING --> CONTRACT_FAILED : **Event:** ContractFailedEvent\n(Condition failed)

note on link
  **Failure Scenarios:**
  - Payment declined
  - Fraud detected
  - Stock unavailable

  Contract cancelled,
  NO ORDER CREATED
end note

state CONTRACT_READY <<Contract>> {
  state "CONTRACT: READY_TO_COMMIT\n(All conditions met,\nready for order creation)" as CR

  note right of CR
    **Ready for Order Creation:**

    All conditions fulfilled:
    ✓ Payment authorized
    ✓ Fraud check passed
    ✓ Stock reserved

    Contract state:
    - OXSTATE = 'ready_to_commit'
    - OXORDERID = NULL (still!)
    - OXCONDITIONS = [all fulfilled]

    **Next:** Create oxorder
  end note
}

CR : **Optimal Order Creation Point**
CR : All risks mitigated, safe to create order

note as N_PHASE2
  **PHASE 2: ORDER CREATION (Commitment Point)**
  Order created when all contract conditions are met
end note

CONTRACT_READY --> CONTRACT_COMMITTED : **Event:** OrderCreatedFromContractEvent\n(Order created, contract committed)

note on link
  **Order Creation:**

  OrderCreationHandler:
  1. Creates oxorder (state: NOT_FINISHED)
  2. Assigns order number
  3. Links contract to order
  4. Contract.commitToOrder(orderId)

  NOW:
  - Contract.OXORDERID = order.OXID ✓
  - Order exists in database ✓
  - Order number assigned ✓
  - No gaps in order numbers! ✓
end note

state CONTRACT_COMMITTED <<Contract>> {
  state "CONTRACT: COMMITTED\n(Order created,\nawaiting payment capture)" as CC

  note right of CC
    **Contract Committed to Order:**

    Database state:
    - Contract.OXSTATE = 'committed'
    - Contract.OXORDERID = 'order123' ✓
    - Order.OXID = 'order123'
    - Order.oxtransstatus = 'NOT_FINISHED'

    **Payment still pending capture!**
    Authorization done, capture needed.
  end note
}

CC : **Contract-Order Link Established**
CC : Contract.OXORDERID → Order.OXID

note as N_PHASE3
  **PHASE 3: ORDER LIFECYCLE (Post-Commitment Phase)**
  Order processes payment capture and fulfillment
end note

state NOT_FINISHED <<Processing>> {
  state "ORDER: NOT_FINISHED\n(Order created,\npayment pending capture)" as NF

  note right of NF
    **Order State:**
    - oxorder.OXID exists ✓
    - oxorder.oxordernr assigned ✓
    - oxorder.oxtransstatus = 'NOT_FINISHED'
    - osc_payment_order_state.OXCONTRACTID set

    **Waiting for:**
    Payment capture (webhook or redirect return)
  end note
}

CONTRACT_COMMITTED --> NOT_FINISHED : Order created

NOT_FINISHED --> IN_PROGRESS : **Event:** PaymentInitiatedEvent\n(Redirect to provider)

state IN_PROGRESS <<Processing>> {
  state "IN_PROGRESS\n(500-800)\nPayment Processing\nat Provider" as IP

  state IP {
    state "500\nExternal Payment" as EP
    state "700\nCard Payment" as CardPay
    state "750\nCard Authorized" as CA
    state "800\nNeed Finalization" as NF2

    [*] --> EP : Redirect payment
    [*] --> CardPay : Card payment
    CardPay --> CA : Authorized
    CA --> NF2 : Finalize
  }

  note right of IP
    **Order Processing States:**

    500 - External (iDEAL, EPS, etc.)
    700 - Card processing (3DS)
    750 - Card authorized
    800 - Need finalization

    **Contract state:**
    Still COMMITTED (waiting for capture)
  end note
}

IN_PROGRESS --> AWAITING_WEBHOOK : **Event:** PaymentApprovedEvent\n(Customer return)

state AWAITING_WEBHOOK <<Waiting>> {
  state "AWAITING_WEBHOOK\n(600)\nWaiting for Provider\nWebhook Confirmation" as AW

  note right of AW
    **Webhook Pending:**

    Customer completed payment at provider,
    now awaiting async webhook confirmation.

    **Contract state:**
    Still COMMITTED (capture pending)

    **Order state:**
    AWAITING_WEBHOOK (600)

    Timeout: 60 minutes
  end note
}

AWAITING_WEBHOOK --> CONTRACT_FULFILLED : **Event:** PaymentCapturedEvent\n(Webhook received)

note on link
  **Webhook Processing:**

  WebhookHandler:
  1. Finds contract by provider order ID
  2. Verifies contract state = COMMITTED
  3. Calls contract.fulfill()
  4. Updates order to OK
  5. Emits ContractFulfilledEvent

  **Contract-Aware Webhooks!**
end note

IN_PROGRESS --> CONTRACT_FULFILLED : **Event:** PaymentCapturedEvent\n(Direct capture)

note on link
  Some payment flows
  capture directly without
  webhook waiting period
end note

state CONTRACT_FULFILLED <<Success>> {
  state "CONTRACT: FULFILLED\n(Payment captured,\ncontract complete)" as CF

  note right of CF
    **Contract Fulfilled:**

    Database state:
    - Contract.OXSTATE = 'fulfilled' ✓
    - Contract.OXFULFILLEDAT = NOW()
    - Order.oxpaid = NOW()
    - Order.oxtransstatus = 'OK'

    **Contract lifecycle complete!**

    Side effects triggered:
    - Email confirmation
    - Inventory update
    - Invoice generation
    - Analytics tracking
  end note
}

CF : **Terminal Success State**

CONTRACT_FULFILLED --> COMPLETED : Order finalized

state COMPLETED <<Success>> {
  state "ORDER: COMPLETED\n(OK)\nOrder Ready for\nFulfillment/Shipping" as SUCCESS

  note right of SUCCESS
    **Order Completed:**

    Final state:
    - Order.oxtransstatus = 'OK' ✓
    - Order.oxpaid = timestamp ✓
    - Contract.OXSTATE = 'fulfilled' ✓

    **Ready for:**
    - Shipment processing
    - Invoice generation
    - Customer service

    Cannot be cancelled
  end note
}

COMPLETED --> [*]

note as N_PHASE4
  **PHASE 4: ERROR & CANCELLATION PATHS**
  Handling failures and cancellations at any stage
end note

CONTRACT_FAILED --> CONTRACT_CANCELLED : Contract cancelled

state CONTRACT_FAILED <<Error>> {
  state "CONTRACT: FAILED\n(Condition failed)" as CFail

  note right of CFail
    **Contract Failed:**

    Reasons:
    - Payment declined
    - Fraud detected (high risk)
    - Stock unavailable
    - Address validation failed

    Contract state:
    - OXSTATE = 'failed'
    - OXSTATEREASON = "reason"
    - OXORDERID = NULL (no order created!)

    **Clean failure - no orphan order**
  end note
}

state CONTRACT_CANCELLED <<Error>> {
  state "CANCELLED\n(Contract/Order cancelled)" as CANCEL

  note right of CANCEL
    **Cancellation:**

    Can occur at:
    1. Contract level (before order)
       → Contract.OXSTATE = 'cancelled'
       → No order exists

    2. Order level (after commitment)
       → Contract.OXSTATE = 'cancelled'
       → Order.OXSTORNO = 1

    Clean cancellation with full audit trail
  end note
}

NOT_FINISHED --> CONTRACT_CANCELLED : **Event:** OrderCancelledEvent
IN_PROGRESS --> CONTRACT_CANCELLED : **Event:** PaymentFailedEvent
AWAITING_WEBHOOK --> CONTRACT_CANCELLED : **Event:** PaymentFailedEvent

note on link
  **Cancellation After Order Created:**

  If order exists:
  1. Cancel contract
  2. Mark order as storno
  3. Cancel at provider
  4. Emit OrderCancelledEvent
end note

AWAITING_WEBHOOK --> TIMEOUT : 60 min timeout

state TIMEOUT <<Processing>> {
  state "TIMEOUT\n(900)\nWebhook Timeout\n(Fallback)" as TO

  note right of TO
    **Webhook Timeout:**

    No webhook received within 60 minutes.

    Fallback actions:
    1. Poll provider API
    2. Check payment status
    3. Either fulfill or cancel

    Contract state: Still COMMITTED
    (polling to determine outcome)
  end note
}

TIMEOUT --> CONTRACT_FULFILLED : **Event:** PaymentCapturedEvent\n(Polling confirmed)
TIMEOUT --> CONTRACT_CANCELLED : **Event:** OrderCancelledEvent\n(Polling failed)

CONTRACT_CANCELLED --> [*]

note bottom
  **Smart-Contract State Machine Benefits:**

  ✅ **Delayed Order Creation:**
     Order created ONLY when all conditions met
     → No orphan orders for failed payments
     → No gaps in order numbers

  ✅ **Explicit Condition Tracking:**
     All preconditions (payment, fraud, stock) tracked in contract
     → Complete audit trail
     → Transparent to customer ("Checking payment...")

  ✅ **Clean Cancellation:**
     Cancel contract vs. delete/rollback order
     → Simpler error handling
     → No database cleanup issues

  ✅ **Contract-Aware Webhooks:**
     Webhook finds contract by provider order ID
     → Verifies contract state = COMMITTED
     → Idempotency guaranteed (state machine prevents duplicates)

  ✅ **Separation of Concerns:**
     Contract = Payment lifecycle (DRAFT → FULFILLED)
     Order = Fulfillment lifecycle (NOT_FINISHED → OK)
     → Clear ownership, easier to maintain

  ✅ **Provider-Agnostic:**
     Works with Stripe, PayPal, Adyen, Unzer, Klarna, Amazon Pay, Square
     → Maps provider states to contract states
     → Consistent architecture across providers

  **State Storage:**
  - Contract state: osc_payment_contract.OXSTATE
  - Order state: oxorder.oxtransstatus + osc_payment_order_state.OXPAYMENTSTATE
  - Link: osc_payment_order_state.OXCONTRACTID → osc_payment_contract.OXID

  **Event-Driven:**
  All state transitions triggered by events
  Multiple subscribers react to ContractFulfilledEvent
end note

note as N_STATES
  **State Mapping:**

  **Contract States (osc_payment_contract.OXSTATE):**
  • draft - Contract created, conditions defined
  • pending - Conditions being resolved
  • ready_to_commit - All conditions met
  • committed - Order created, linked to contract
  • fulfilled - Payment captured, contract complete
  • cancelled - Contract cancelled (any phase)
  • expired - Contract expired (no action within 24h)
  • failed - Condition failed (payment declined, etc.)

  **Order States (oxorder.oxtransstatus):**
  • NOT_FINISHED - Order created, payment pending
  • OK - Order completed, ready for fulfillment
  • (500-900 states now in osc_payment_order_state)

  **Critical Difference:**
  OLD: Order exists from "Place Order" click
  NEW: Order exists only when contract committed
end note

note as N_FLOW
  **Complete Flow Example:**

  1. User clicks "Place Order"
     → Contract DRAFT created

  2. Contract transitions to PENDING
     → PaymentAuthorizationHandler: Authorize payment ✓
     → FraudCheckHandler: Check fraud ✓
     → StockReservationHandler: Reserve stock ✓

  3. All conditions fulfilled
     → Contract transitions to READY_TO_COMMIT

  4. OrderCreationHandler triggered
     → Creates oxorder (NOT_FINISHED)
     → Contract transitions to COMMITTED
     → Contract.OXORDERID = order.OXID

  5. Customer redirected to provider
     → Order state: IN_PROGRESS (500-800)

  6. Customer completes payment
     → Order state: AWAITING_WEBHOOK (600)

  7. Webhook received
     → Contract transitions to FULFILLED
     → Order state: OK
     → ContractFulfilledEvent emitted

  8. Side effects triggered
     → Email sent
     → Inventory updated
     → Invoice generated
end note

@enduml
